# KDE Plasma 6 Wayland Suite — Cursor CLI Rules

You have access to the `kde-wayland-suite` in this repository.

When the user asks about keyboard layouts (ABNT2, US-intl, cedilla), broken
shortcuts (Ctrl+C / Ctrl+V stopping system-wide), touchpad gestures, the
Logitech MX Master 3S, or battery/power consumption in KDE Plasma 6 Wayland:

1. Full diagnostic:
   `./bin/kde-config status` or `make check`
2. Fix keyboard shortcuts and cedilla support (US-intl, Chrome, Orca, Electron, GTK, Qt):
   `./bin/kde-config fix-keyboard` or `make fix-keyboard`
3. Touchpad gestures (libinput-gestures):
   `./bin/kde-config gestures` or `make gestures`
4. Logitech MX Master 3S (logiops):
   `./bin/kde-config mouse` or `make mouse`
5. Battery/power diagnostic (read-only):
   `./bin/kde-config battery-status` or `make battery-status`
6. Switch active keyboard layout:
   `./bin/kde-config switch br` or `./bin/kde-config switch us`

Never apply a battery fix without asking the user first — `battery-apply` only
acts on the `BATTERY_FIX_*` variables you pass, and each one is opt-in.
`battery-revert` undoes the last application.

Report every command using the standardized output format defined in
`base/shared/OUTPUT-CONTRACT.md`: **Plano** → **Execução** → **Resumo**. It is
identical across Claude Code, Cursor, OMP, OpenCode and Antigravity.
